  "body": "Rescues the stdio MCP hardening left uncommitted in the stale `issue/128-mcp-server` worktree (part of #128) onto current main.\n\n## What changed\n- `crates/app/src/mcp/mod.rs`: a request with `\"id\": null` is refused as an invalid request (-32600). `serve()` reads each line as bytes through a 16 MiB cap (`MAX_LINE_BYTES`); an oversize line is a parse error (-32700) and the rest of it is skipped buffer by buffer without being held in memory; a non-UTF-8 line is a parse error and the session reads on. Only an I/O failure of the streams ends the loop early.\n- `crates/app/src/mcp/edit.rs`: a misspelled field at any depth of a params patch is refused naming its dotted path (`unknown field clearance_z.ofset`); previously only top-level typos were caught and nested ones were silently dropped by serde.\n- `crates/app/src/mcp/tools.rs`: `post` reports the path `v_post` actually wrote, not the path asked for.\n\n## How tested\nOwn worktree + own target dir, on origin/main fc9b297:\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test mcp`: 8/8 pass, pinned by `a_nested_patch_typo_is_refused_by_its_path`, `a_null_id_is_an_invalid_request`, `a_non_utf8_line_is_a_parse_error_and_the_session_reads_on`, `an_oversized_line_is_a_parse_error_and_is_skipped`\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --lib`: 95/95 pass\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean\n\n## Not exercised\n- No real MCP client session over a pipe (the tests drive `serve()` over in-memory byte slices).\n- The `post` path change has no dedicated assertion of its own beyond the existing whole-job test.\n\n## Overlap\nFork PRs #421, #422 and #428 also edit `crates/app/src/mcp/mod.rs` and `tools.rs`; whichever lands second resolves the conflict (keep both sides).\n\nChangelog: MCP stdio server refuses null request ids, survives oversize and non-UTF-8 lines, names nested params-patch typos by path, and reports the post path actually written\n\nFixes #443\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
